Drop --ram-only-header from the ESP32-S3 elf2image command line

tools/esp32s3/Config.mk

WHY
---
`tools/esp32s3/Config.mk` appends `--ram-only-header` to the `elf2image`
command line whenever `CONFIG_ESPRESSIF_SIMPLE_BOOT=y`:

  $(eval ELF2IMAGE_OPTS := $(if $(CONFIG_ESPRESSIF_SIMPLE_BOOT),--ram-only-header) \
       -fs $(FLASH_SIZE) -fm $(FLASH_MODE) -ff $(FLASH_FREQ))

`--ram-only-header` tells `elf2image` to describe ONLY the RAM (IRAM/DRAM)
segments in the image header and to hide the XIP (IROM/DROM) segments.  The
result is a 2-segment image whose header carries no loadable XIP segment for
the ROM to act on.

Measured on the AI-VOX3 board (ESP32-S3, ROM banner `ESP-ROM:esp32s3-20210327`):

  run#55/56  (--ram-only-header active)  -> segcount=2, flashed at 0x0
                serial: 0 BYTES (completely silent -- not even the ROM banner)
  run#52     (no --ram-only-header)      -> segcount=5, flashed at 0x0
                serial: 24364 bytes -> `entry 0x40374af0` -> IllegalInstruction

i.e. with a 2-segment (ram-only) image this board's ROM reads the image header,
finds no loadable segment and gives up BEFORE it prints anything -- not even
its own `ESP-ROM:` banner.  The flag is SIMPLE_BOOT's intended design, but this
particular ROM revision does not cooperate with it, so the 2-segment image can
never boot here.  The 5-segment image is the only path that even reaches
`entry`; the remaining crash on that path is a separate XIP issue handled by
0001-esp_loader-map_rom_segments-override-irom-drom-size.patch.

FIX
---
Remove the conditional `$(if $(CONFIG_ESPRESSIF_SIMPLE_BOOT),--ram-only-header)`
block so the elf2image command line is just the plain flash geometry:

  $(eval ELF2IMAGE_OPTS := -fs $(FLASH_SIZE) -fm $(FLASH_MODE) -ff $(FLASH_FREQ))

This makes MKIMAGE emit a normal 5-segment image (DROM + IROM visible in the
header) that the board's ROM accepts and jumps into, exactly as run#52 did.

Scope: esp32s3 ONLY.  tools/espressif/Config.mk, tools/esp32s2/Config.mk and
tools/esp32/Config.mk contain the same `$(if ...)` line, but those chips are
not used by this board and are deliberately left untouched to keep the change
minimal and low-risk.  Verified only tools/esp32s3/Config.mk matches.

--- a/tools/esp32s3/Config.mk
+++ b/tools/esp32s3/Config.mk
@@ -186,5 +186,5 @@ define MKIMAGE
 		exit 1; \
 	fi
-	$(eval ELF2IMAGE_OPTS := $(if $(CONFIG_ESPRESSIF_SIMPLE_BOOT),--ram-only-header) -fs $(FLASH_SIZE) -fm $(FLASH_MODE) -ff $(FLASH_FREQ))
+	$(eval ELF2IMAGE_OPTS := -fs $(FLASH_SIZE) -fm $(FLASH_MODE) -ff $(FLASH_FREQ))
 	esptool.py -c esp32s3 elf2image $(ELF2IMAGE_OPTS) -o nuttx.bin nuttx
 	$(Q) echo nuttx.bin >> nuttx.manifest
